KG42.register("rules-a2f9789d6ec41bce44e5faf5",{"id":"45-heat_pump_flexibility::v141-c-R006","paper":"45-heat_pump_flexibility","record":{"rule_id":"v141-c-R006","mechanism_id":"v141-a-M01","name":"Price-signal coordination","process_stage":"coordination","market_meaning":"The local market closing price is communicated to each agent as the participant price signal. Scope: Proposed centralized two-sided local energy market; communication of market closing prices to participant agents.","independence_rationale":"Relations governed by the approved function coordination.price_signal under the fixed relation-ownership template. Conditional branches retain their explicit scope in local constraints.","V":["coordination.price_signal","pricing.local"],"E":[{"edge_id":"v141-c-R006-E001","source":"pricing.local","target":"coordination.price_signal","type":"links","constraint_ids":["v141-c-R006-C001"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-e10"]}],"omega":{"market_type":"LEM","network_level":null,"jurisdiction":null,"pricing_scope":null,"time_scale":null,"participant_types":[],"trading_stage":"coordination","context_text":"Proposed centralized two-sided local energy market; communication of market closing prices to participant agents.","unknown_fields":["network_level","jurisdiction","pricing_scope","time_scale","participant_types"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-e10"]},"x":[],"theta":[],"phi":[{"constraint_id":"v141-c-R006-C001","kind":"procedural","role":"core","statement":"The local market closing price is communicated to each agent as the participant price signal. Scope: Proposed centralized two-sided local energy market; communication of market closing prices to participant agents.","expression":null,"formalization_origin":"not_formalized","template_id":null,"members":["pricing.local","coordination.price_signal"],"variable_refs":[],"parameter_refs":[],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-e10"]}],"pi":[{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g01-e10","location":{"location_id":"src-115be449fd-p04-c1r4__v141-a-M01-clearing","page":4,"printed_page":null,"section":null,"anchor_text":"interval in a standardized bid format. The objective of the market is 𝛥𝑝 to maximize social welfare ","equation_id":"1","figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-04.png","occurrence_role":"formula"},"source_text":"The bids and offers are denoted as d_i and s_j, respectively. n_B and n_S represent the number of buyers and sellers. To achieve maximum social welfare, the market operator organizes the bids in decreasing order and offers in increasing order, establishing the demand and supply curve. The intersection of the demand and supply curve is known as the market closing price, which is then communicated to each agent and used for settlement."}],"field_notes":{"empty_E_reason":null,"empty_x_reason":"No decision variable is defined for the communication act in the supplied source. The market closing price is an endogenous clearing outcome from pricing.local, and the recipient agents are not typed as a set in the frozen graph; declaring an agent-indexed signal variable would invent a domain not supplied by the source.","empty_theta_reason":"No numeric or fixed parameter is defined by the source for this communication step. 'Market closing price' is an endogenous outcome rather than a fixed parameter, and the source supplies no price-signal symbol, unit, or constant for the communication rule."},"evidence_basis":"explicit","implementation_status":"unimplemented","status":"needs_review","lead_ids":["v141-a-M01-clearing","v141-a-M01-matching","v141-a-M01-pricing","v141-a-M01-settlement"],"extras":{"decision_anchor":"coordination.price_signal","graph_fact_supports":[[{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g01-e10","quote":"The intersection of the demand and supply curve is known as the market closing price, which is then communicated to each agent and used for settlement."}]],"C2_formalization":{"graph_sha256":"4a87b357b7349ee8136d7cadb12b08d5baee8f11753a1f9124c8ae667ab2f78c","applicability":"non_mathematical","reason":"The frozen rule expresses a procedural communication step: the already-determined local market closing price is transmitted from pricing.local to coordination.price_signal for each agent. The supplied source text states that the intersection of the demand and supply curves is the market closing price and that this price is then communicated to each agent and used for settlement. It does not define a decision variable, fixed parameter, agent index set, price-signal symbol, or algebraic relation for the communication act itself. Treating this as a mathematical rule would require inventing a symbol/domain for the price signal or agent set not present in the frozen graph.","bindings":[{"object_id":"v141-c-R006-C001","node_ids":["pricing.local","coordination.price_signal"],"edge_ids":["v141-c-R006-E001"],"rationale":"Constraint C001 is exactly the procedural link represented by frozen edge E001: the source states that the local market closing price is communicated to each agent as the participant price signal. The source evidence v141-b-g01-e10 supports only this communication step, not an algebraic broadcast formula or a typed set of recipient agents."}],"revision_requests":[]}},"quarantined_references":[]}});
